  {
   "kind": "heading",
   "text": "Frequently Asked Questions",
   "level": 2,
   "meta": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": "heading",
   "text": "Who is this course for?",
   "level": 3,
   "meta": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "text": "This course is designed for students with programming experience (CS111 equivalent) who want to learn how to leverage modern AI tools to dramatically improve their software development productivity. CS221/229 is recommended but not required.",
   "level": 0,
   "meta": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": "heading",
   "text": "What will I build in this course?",
   "level": 3,
   "meta": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "text": "Students will complete weekly hands-on assignments covering LLM prompting, MCP server development, AI IDE usage, Claude Code workflows, security analysis, code review automation, and full-stack web applications. The course culminates in a final project showcasing modern development practices.",
   "level": 0,
   "meta": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": "heading",
   "text": "What tools will we use?",
   "level": 3,
   "meta": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "text": "The course covers a range of AI development tools including Claude Code, Warp terminal, Cursor/Windsurf IDEs, Semgrep, Graphite, and Vercel. We'll also work with the Model Context Protocol (MCP) and various LLM APIs.",
   "level": 0,
   "meta": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": "heading",
   "text": "How are grades determined?",
   "level": 3,
   "meta": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "text": "Grades are based on weekly assignments, participation in class discussions, and the final project. See the assignment calendar for specific deadlines.",
   "level": 0,
   "meta": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": "heading",
   "text": "Are lectures recorded?",
   "level": 3,
   "meta": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "text": "Please check with the course staff for recording availability. Slides for each lecture are linked in the syllabus above.",
   "level": 0,
   "meta": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": "heading",
   "text": "How do I contact the teaching team?",
   "level": 3,
